# No commit or push without an explicit request

This rule applies in every session.

- Do not run `git commit` unless the user explicitly asks for a commit in that message.
- Do not run `git push`, including a normal push, `--force`, or `--force-with-lease`, unless the user explicitly asks for a push in that message.
- Do not treat "fix it", "ship it", "save it", or finishing a task as permission to commit or push.
- Leave changes in the working tree until the user asks.
